1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,858
America and Britain almost went to war.

2
00:00:02,906 --> 00:00:04,519
Over one pig.

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,774
A farmer caught it eating his potatoes.

4
00:00:06,792 --> 00:00:08,123
So he shot it.

5
00:00:08,151 --> 00:00:08,443
Problem:

6
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:10,128
the farmer was American.

7
00:00:10,147 --> 00:00:11,821
The pig was British.

8
00:00:11,981 --> 00:00:13,282
He offered ten dollars.

9
00:00:13,301 --> 00:00:15,038
The owner wanted a hundred.

10
00:00:15,189 --> 00:00:17,666
Worse, both countries claimed the island.

11
00:00:17,774 --> 00:00:20,311
America sent over four hundred soldiers.

12
00:00:20,575 --> 00:00:22,537
Britain sent five warships.

13
00:00:22,642 --> 00:00:24,726
The governor wanted the Americans gone.

14
00:00:24,868 --> 00:00:26,330
The admiral said no.

15
00:00:26,349 --> 00:00:27,566
Not over a pig.

16
00:00:28,009 --> 00:00:29,879
So both sides just stayed.

17
00:00:29,898 --> 00:00:31,393
For twelve years.

18
00:00:31,575 --> 00:00:32,679
And partied together.

19
00:00:32,792 --> 00:00:34,872
Then a German emperor settled it.

20
00:00:34,943 --> 00:00:36,613
The island went to America.

21
00:00:36,632 --> 00:00:37,821
Total casualties:

22
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:38,783
one pig.

23
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,698
Team farmer, or team pig?
